 "body": "## What\n\n`ClaudeCliEngine.parse` decided \"the account is out of quota\" by searching the **entire** JSON envelope for three substrings, including `structured_output` \u2014 the findings the model wrote about the tree under review. A finding that quotes `rate_limit_error` (an ordinary identifier to find in code) raised `UsageLimited` from a clean, successful review.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`UsageLimited` trips `Governor.trip`: every claim on the shared store is refused for five hours and the calibration is cut by 10 %. The trigger is released *unattempted*, so it is re-claimed after the hold, re-reviewed and trips again. Anyone whose code gets reviewed could take the reviewer offline for the whole fleet with one line in a diff \u2014 and the review that tripped it had already spent real tokens.\n\n## How\n\n`_envelope_usage_limited` replaces `usage_limited(json.dumps(envelope))`:\n\n- the envelope is asked **only when it says it errored** \u2014 `is_error is True` or a `subtype` starting with `error_`;\n- only the CLI's own error-carrying fields are read: `error`, `result`, `subtype`;\n- `structured_output`, `usage` and `modelUsage` are never matched.\n\nThe stderr path in `CliEngine.run` is unchanged \u2014 stderr is the CLI's own channel and was already narrow.\n\nItem 4 of the issue (rate-limiting the breaker against a poison dedupe key) is deliberately **not** in this PR: it is a separate availability behaviour with its own bound to pin, and the false positive is what made a poison PR possible in the first place.\n\n## Tests\n\nThree new tests in `tests/test_cli_engine.py`, verified to fail on the parent commit:\n\n- a `success` envelope whose finding title *and* body contain every marker parses to `Outcome.COMPLETED` with its finding intact;\n- a marker in `result` on a non-errored envelope is not a usage limit;\n- an `is_error: true` envelope with a marker in `result` **still** raises `UsageLimited`, even with a marker-quoting finding present.\n\n## Gate\n\n```\n1014 passed, 2 skipped, 1 deselected, 1 warning in 74.01s\n79 files already formatted   /   ruff check: All checks passed!\npylint src 9.95/10   pylint tests 9.36/10\npyright: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 informations\n```\n\nReleases **1.1.1**.\n\nFixes #61.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
